.TH GIT-WC 1
.SH NAME
git-wc \- clean linked worktrees whose branches are already merged
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git wc
.RI [ target-branch ]
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git wc
removes linked worktrees whose branch is already merged into
.BI origin/ target-branch ,
then deletes that local branch.
It detects regular merges (ancestor) and rebase/squash merges
.RB ( git\ cherry
patch equivalence).
When
.I target-branch
is omitted, the remote default branch from
.B origin/HEAD
is used.
.PP
Stale worktree registrations (missing on disk) are pruned first.
.PP
Never removes the main worktree, the current worktree, worktrees on protected
branches
.RB ( main ,
.BR master ,
.BR develop ,
.BR dev ,
target), or detached-HEAD worktrees.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry-run
Show worktrees that would be removed without removing them.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git wc --dry-run
    Preview worktree cleanup against the remote default branch.

git wc
    Remove merged worktrees and delete their branches.

git wc develop --dry-run
    Preview cleanup against origin/develop.
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-bc (1)
